  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected: the *unto* of *unto her* was given to the object suffix under rule 18. Rule 18 places the pronoun that realizes a suffix, and rule 44 places a preposition the ASV supplies to reach a bare direct object on the verb's unit, so *unto* joins יִבְּמָהּ's rendering and the suffix keeps *her*.",
    "הַחוּצָה is read as an article whose *the* the ASV does not write (rule 29) beside a host-plus-directive-he fusion on *without* (rules 30, 32).",
    "The head of *perform the duty of a husband’s brother* stays on *duty* as the light verb's complement; *brother* was the defensible alternative."
  ]
